<title>BELGIUM: AEA Jan-Sep traffic higher on most routes.</title>
<headline>AEA Jan-Sep traffic higher on most routes.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Association of European Airlines (AEA) traffic update for the period January to September shows volume increases in most markets except the intra-European trade.</p>
<p>A statement from the association shows that only intra-European traffic has seen a slight decline, slipping 0.9 percent to 658.9 million revenue freight tonne kilometres (RTKF) for the period Jan-Sep 1996, compared to the same period last year.</p>
<p>Europe to North Africa and the Middle East and Europe to the Far East and Australasia were the sectors that showed the strongest growth, increasing by 15.5 percent and 10.2 percent respectively.</p>
<p>  Region			    Million RTKF	% Change on</p>
<p>   Geographical Europe	     658.9		-0.9</p>
<p>   Europe-N Africa/M East	  740.6		15.5</p>
<p>   North Atlantic		  6,151.0		 0.5</p>
<p>   Europe-Far East/Australasia 6,521.1		10.2</p>
<p>   Europe-Sub Saharan Africa   1,991.7		 2.1</p>
<p>   South Atlantic		    948.3		 6.4</p>
<p>   Mid Atlantic			860.0		 5.5</p>
<p>   Total longhaul		 15,874.3		 4.6</p>
<p>   Total international	  17,273.8		 4.8</p>
<p>*These figures relate to the international scheduled services of AEA member airlines.</p>
